values ('f0a1b2c3-4d5e-4f52-9c12-2d3e4f5a6b82', '3-d-design-foundation-year', '3-D Design (Foundation Year)', '3-D Design (Foundation Year) studies how form, space, gravity, scale, structure, and viewer movement shape three-dimensional work. Students work with solid form, void, weight, density, volume, contour, and proportion; negative space, site, and installation; materials and their associations; cutting, joinery, and load-bearing stability; additive and subtractive processes; casting and molding; found objects, assemblage, and object meaning; surface and finish as conceptual decisions; research through maquettes and revision; critique, documentation, and presentation; and a final project that synthesizes form, material, space, concept, craft, and documentation.');

